<GuideLayout 
  title="The Science of Compression: Why 230GSM Interlock is the Professional Choice"
  type="FABRIC TECH"
  date="June 28, 2026"
  readTime="10 min read"
>
  <p>In the world of high-performance leggings, not all fabrics are created equal. For professional brand owners, understanding "GSM" (Grams per Square Meter) and the "Interlock" knit structure is the difference between a see-through product and a premium, squat-proof garment.</p>
  
  <h2>What is 230GSM Interlock?</h2>
  <p>Most entry-level activewear uses lightweight single-jersey fabric. While thin, it often fails the "squat test." At FITCLO, our premium collections feature <strong>230GSM Interlock</strong> fabric—a double-knit structure that provides maximum opacity and multi-directional compression.</p>
  
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Squat-Proof Security:</strong> The higher density ensures total coverage, even under maximum stretch.</li>
    <li><strong>Muscle Support:</strong> 230GSM provides the "sculpting" effect that customers look for in high-end fitness brands.</li>
    <li><strong>Durability:</strong> The Interlock structure prevents rolling at the edges and maintains its shape after hundreds of wash cycles.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Technical Composition for 2026</h2>
  <p>We combine this density with a 80% Nylon / 20% Spandex ratio. This specific blend offers the "buttery soft" hand-feel popularized by top global brands while providing the structural integrity required for intense training. When sourcing for your next collection, look beyond the price and ask for the GSM—it is the true metric of quality.</p>
</GuideLayout>
